2:{t:"Ism-e-Khaas and Ism-e-Aam",
en:"<b>Ism-e-Khaas</b> (proper noun) names one particular person or being, such as Allah or a Prophet. <b>Ism-e-Aam</b> (common noun) names a whole kind of thing, such as a book, a man or people. Adding ال (al-) makes a common noun definite, but it stays a common noun.",
ur:"اسمِ خاص کسی ایک معین شخص یا ذات کا نام ہوتا ہے، جیسے اللہ یا کسی نبی کا نام۔ اسمِ عام پوری جنس کا نام ہوتا ہے، جیسے کتاب، آدمی، لوگ۔ ال لگنے سے اسمِ عام معرفہ بنتا ہے مگر خاص نہیں ہوتا۔",
ex:[[112,1,"الله","Ism-e-Khaas","The name of one particular Being, Allah."],[20,9,"موسى","Ism-e-Khaas","The name of one particular Prophet."],[19,16,"مريم","Ism-e-Khaas","The name of one particular person."],[2,2,"الكتاب","Ism-e-Aam","It names a kind of thing (a book). The al- only makes it definite."],[28,20,"رجل","Ism-e-Aam","It names any man, not one named person."],[114,1,"الناس","Ism-e-Aam","It names a whole group: people."]],
q:[[20,9,"موسى","Which type of ism is {w}?",YN,0,"It is the name of one particular Prophet, so it is Ism-e-Khaas."],[2,2,"الكتاب","Which type of ism is {w}?",YN,1,"A book is a kind of thing, not one named person, so it is Ism-e-Aam."],[114,1,"الناس","Which type of ism is {w}?",YN,1,"It means people in general, so it is Ism-e-Aam."]]},
3:{t:"Zameer (ضمير)",
en:"A <b>zameer</b> (pronoun) stands in place of a noun. <b>Zameer munfasil</b> is a separate word: huwa (he), hum (they), anta (you), nahnu (we). The marfūʿ munfasil forms work as the subject. <b>Zameer muttasil</b> is joined to another word, like the ka in rabbuka (your Lord).",
ur:"ضمیر وہ لفظ ہے جو اسم کی جگہ آتا ہے۔ ضمیرِ منفصل الگ لفظ ہوتی ہے، جیسے هو، هم، أنت، نحن۔ ضمیرِ مرفوع منفصل عموماً فاعل یا مبتدا بنتی ہے۔ ضمیرِ متصل دوسرے لفظ کے ساتھ جڑی ہوتی ہے، جیسے ربّك میں ك۔",
ex:[[112,1,"هو","Zameer marfūʿ munfasil, 3rd person masculine singular (he)","A separate word, and it is the subject of the sentence."],[2,5,"هم","Zameer marfūʿ munfasil, 3rd person masculine plural (they)","A separate word meaning they."],[2,32,"أنت","Zameer marfūʿ munfasil, 2nd person masculine singular (you)","A separate word meaning you."],[2,30,"ونحن","Wāw + zameer marfūʿ munfasil, 1st person plural (we)","The wāw means and; nahnu is a separate word meaning we."],[93,3,"ربك","Ism with zameer muttasil (ka, your)","The ka is joined to the noun, so it is muttasil."]],
q:[[112,1,"هو","What is {w}?",["Zameer munfasil","Zameer muttasil","Ism-e-Ishara","Harf-e-Jar"],0,"It is a separate pronoun meaning he."],[93,3,"ربك","The ك at the end of {w} is…",["Zameer muttasil","Zameer munfasil","Fiʿl","Harf-e-Jar"],0,"It is joined to the noun, so it is a muttasil pronoun meaning your."],[2,32,"أنت","Which person and number is {w}?",["2nd person singular (you)","3rd person singular (he)","1st person plural (we)","3rd person plural (they)"],0,"Anta means you (one person, masculine)."]]},
4:{t:"Ism-e-Ishara",
en:"<b>Ism-e-Ishara</b> (demonstrative pronoun) points to something: <i>dhālika</i> (that, far, masculine), <i>tilka</i> (that, far, feminine), <i>hādhā</i> (this, near, masculine) and <i>ulāʾika</i> (those, plural). It is a noun, so it can be the subject of a sentence.",
ur:"اسمِ اشارہ وہ اسم ہے جس سے کسی چیز کی طرف اشارہ کیا جائے۔ ذلك (وہ، دور کے لیے مذکر)، تلك (وہ، دور کے لیے مؤنث)، هذا (یہ، قریب کے لیے مذکر)، أولئك (وہ لوگ، جمع)۔",
ex:[[2,2,"ذلك","Ism-e-Ishara, far, masculine singular","It points to something far away: that (Book)."],[2,134,"تلك","Ism-e-Ishara, far, feminine singular","It points to a feminine thing (ummah, a nation): that."],[3,62,"هذا","Ism-e-Ishara, near, masculine singular","It points to something near: this."],[2,5,"أولئك","Ism-e-Ishara, plural (those)","It points to a group of people: those."]],
q:[[2,2,"ذلك","{w} points to…",["Something far, masculine","Something near, masculine","A group of people","A feminine thing nearby"],0,"Dhālika is for something far, masculine, singular."],[3,62,"هذا","What does {w} mean?",["this","that (far)","those","we"],0,"Hādhā means this, for something near."],[2,5,"أولئك","{w} is used for…",["A plural group","One masculine thing","One feminine thing","An action"],0,"Ulāʾika means those, for a group."]]},
5:{t:"Harf-e-Jar and Ism-e-Majroor",
en:"<b>Harf-e-Jar</b> (preposition) is a particle placed before a noun that puts it in jarr (usually a kasra). Common ones: min (from), ilā (to), ʿalā (on), fī (in), bi (with, by) and li (for). The noun after it is the <b>Ism-e-Majroor</b>. Its sign is usually a kasra, or kasratayn when indefinite.",
ur:"حرفِ جر وہ حرف ہے جو اسم سے پہلے آ کر اسے جر (زیر) دیتا ہے۔ عام حروفِ جر: مِن، إلى، على، في، بِ، لِ۔ جس اسم کو جر ملے اسے اسمِ مجرور کہتے ہیں اور اس کی عام علامت زیر ہے۔",
ex:[[2,10,"في","Harf-e-Jar","A particle meaning in. It puts the next noun in jarr."],[2,10,"قلوبهم","Ism-e-Majroor","It comes right after fī, so it is majroor. The hum at the end is attached to it."],[17,1,"إلى","Harf-e-Jar","A particle meaning to. The noun after it is majroor."],[17,1,"بعبده","Harf-e-Jar bi + Ism-e-Majroor","The bi is a harf-e-jar; ʿabd (servant) after it is majroor."],[2,5,"على","Harf-e-Jar","A particle meaning on, upon."],[2,5,"هدى","Ism-e-Majroor","It follows ʿalā, so it is majroor. The mark is hidden on the final letter."]],
q:[[2,10,"في","What is {w}?",["Harf-e-Jar","Ism-e-Ishara","Zameer munfasil","Fiʿl"],0,"Fī (in) is a preposition, so it is a harf-e-jar."],[2,10,"قلوبهم","Why is {w} majroor?",["It comes after a harf-e-jar (fī)","It is the subject","It is a verb","It starts the sentence"],0,"A noun directly after a harf-e-jar is in jarr."],[17,1,"إلى","What does {w} mean?",["to","from","on","in"],0,"Ilā means to."]]},
6:{t:"Huruf Mushabbaha bil-Fiʿl",
en:"<b>Huruf Mushabbaha bil-Fiʿl</b> (letters that resemble the verb) are inna, anna, ka-anna, lākinna, laita and laʿalla. They enter a nominal sentence (mubtada’ and khabar). The first noun becomes their <b>ism</b> and takes naṣb (fatḥa); the second stays marfūʿ and is their <b>khabar</b>. Meanings: inna/anna = indeed, that; ka-anna = as if; laita = if only; laʿalla = perhaps, so that.",
ur:"یہ حروف فعل سے مشابہت رکھتے ہیں اور جملہ اسمیہ پر آتے ہیں۔ یہ مبتدا کو نصب دیتے ہیں (اسم) اور خبر کو رفع (خبر)۔ إنّ/أنّ = بے شک، كأنّ = گویا، ليت = کاش، لعلّ = شاید/تاکہ۔",
ex:[[2,20,"إن","Harf Mushabbah bil-Fiʿl (inna)","It means indeed. It puts the noun after it in naṣb."],[2,20,"الله","Ism of inna, manṣūb","It is the first noun after inna, so it takes fatḥa. Its khabar (qadīr) stays marfūʿ.",1],[108,1,"إنا","Inna + nā (we)","The nā is attached and acts as the ism of inna."],[2,21,"لعلكم","Laʿalla + kum (you)","It means so that you may. The kum is its ism."],[63,4,"كأنهم","Ka-anna + hum (they)","It means as if they. The hum is its ism."],[78,40,"ليتني","Laita + nī (me)","It means if only. The nī is its ism."]],
q:[[2,20,"إن","What is {w}?",["Harf Mushabbah bil-Fiʿl","Harf-e-Jar","Ism-e-Ishara","Zameer"],0,"Inna is one of the huruf mushabbaha bil-fiʿl."],[63,4,"كأنهم","What does {w} mean?",["as if they","indeed we","if only me","so that you"],0,"Ka-anna means as if; hum means they."],[2,20,"الله","Why is {w} manṣūb after inna?",["It is the ism of inna","It is a verb","It is a harf","It is the khabar"],0,"Inna gives naṣb to the noun that follows it, called its ism.",1]]}
